      "question": {
        ":question/id": "60914be7-a465-5aff-b814-3bacb68173b5",
        ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix $X,$ given by\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & -9 & -5 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-4{R}_{3}$ on $X?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-4{R}_{3}$ means that we need to add $-4$ times the third row to the second row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & -9 & -5 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-4{R}_{3} \\\\  & \\sim\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & -9 & -5 \\\\ 4+(-4)(1) & 1+(-4)(-3) & -4+(-4)(1) \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\sim\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & -9 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 13 & -8 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
