        ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix $X,$ given by\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -7 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -8 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-3{R}_{3}$ on $X?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-3{R}_{3}$ means that we need to add $-3$ times the third row to the first row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -7 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -8 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-3{R}_{3} \\\\  & \\sim\\begin{bmatrix}3+(-3)(1) & -7+(-3)(-1) & 3+(-3)(0) \\\\ -1 & -8 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\sim\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -8 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
